# 🧠 Key Concepts Learned

- Comprehensions allow creating collections using a single line of code.
- List comprehensions simplify the process of creating new lists.
- Dictionary comprehensions create key-value pairs efficiently.
- Set comprehensions generate unique values automatically.
- Generator expressions produce values lazily, making them memory efficient.
- Conditions can be added using `if` and `if...else`.
- Nested comprehensions help work with multi-dimensional data structures.

