# 📌 Important Notes

- List comprehensions use square brackets `[]`.
- Dictionary comprehensions use curly braces `{key: value}`.
- Set comprehensions use curly braces `{}`.
- Generator expressions use parentheses `()`.
- Comprehensions often make code shorter and easier to read.
- Generator expressions consume less memory because values are generated only when needed.

---

# ⚖️ Types of Comprehensions

| Type | Syntax |
|------|--------|
| List Comprehension | `[]` |
| Dictionary Comprehension | `{key: value}` |
| Set Comprehension | `{}` |
| Generator Expression | `()` |

